Zstandard
---------

src/ManagedCompressions.Zstd is an independent implementation of the Zstandard
format (RFC 8878). Its decoding algorithms and its validation follow those of
the reference implementation, libzstd (https://github.com/facebook/zstd), so
that both accept and refuse the same frames. Its compressor reproduces libzstd's
compression parameters, match finders, block splitting and entropy coding, so
that both write the same frames; that part is derived from libzstd 1.5.7 and
remains under its license, quoted below.

ManagedCompressions.Zstd's tests read zstd's golden files (tests/golden-* at
tag v1.5.7) and frames generated by zstd's tests/decodecorpus.c, which
tools/native-ref/testdata.sh writes from the zstd 1.5.7 release. The repository
does not distribute them; they remain under zstd's license.

